cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or code, please cite the article and this repository."
title: "Flower visitors in purpose-designed cover crop mixtures (Amazon–Cerrado transition, Brazil): data and analysis code"
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-4.0
date-released: 2026-11-08
repository-code: "https://github.com/agrocarbon-ufma/pollinators-cover-crop-mixes"
abstract: >-
  Field data and analysis code for a study of flower visitors in three
  purpose-designed cover crop mixtures (Carbon, Pollinator and Multipurpose)
  sown on 19 July 2025 in Chapadinha, Maranhão, Brazil (Amazon–Cerrado
  transition, dry season). The experiment follows a randomized complete block
  design with 4 blocks and 24 plots of 5 × 5 m. Flower visitors were counted
  visually by morphogroup in 13 timed observations (4 min per plot) from
  24 August to 1 October 2025, together with air temperature, relative
  humidity, wind speed and light intensity. Cover crop fresh biomass per plot
  is also included. The analysis notebook (Python runtime with R cells)
  reproduces all statistical tables and figures from the raw files. Data are
  licensed CC BY 4.0; code is licensed MIT (see LICENSE.txt).
